  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "| $y$ | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)$ | $0.25$ | $0.6$ | $0.15$ |\n\nFind the $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=3]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)$ is shown in the table above.",
  "worked_solution": "The conditional expected value of  $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=3] & ={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0.25+3\\cdot 0.6+5\\cdot 0.15 \\\\  & =3.05.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
